From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Piyush Jena <jepiyush@amazon.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] retain .data.rel.ro.local in the FIPS shared link for GCC 14

GCC 14 places read-only data that requires a dynamic relocation into
.data.rel.ro.local, where GCC 13 left it in .rodata. In bcm.o this is a
table of 83 pointers into .text, i.e. the static function pointer tables
in the module.

gcc_fips_shared.lds discards every other section as a tripwire, so the
partial link now fails with one error per reference:

  `.data.rel.ro.local' referenced in section `.text' of
  libbcm_library.a(bcm.c.o): defined in discarded section
  `.data.rel.ro.local' of libbcm_library.a(bcm.c.o)

Give the section its own output section rather than discarding it.
Output section matching is first-match-wins, so the broader *(*.data.*)
discard still catches anything unexpected and the tripwire is preserved.

The integrity hash is unaffected: util/fipstools/inject_hash hashes only
.text and .rodata, bounded by the BORINGSSL_bcm_{text,rodata}_{start,end}
markers, and the retained section lies outside both. That is also the
correct place for data the dynamic linker rewrites, since bytes covered
by the hash must be identical at build time and at startup.

Signed-off-by: Piyush Jena <jepiyush@amazon.com>
---
 crypto/fipsmodule/gcc_fips_shared.lds | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crypto/fipsmodule/gcc_fips_shared.lds b/crypto/fipsmodule/gcc_fips_shared.lds
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/crypto/fipsmodule/gcc_fips_shared.lds
+++ b/crypto/fipsmodule/gcc_fips_shared.lds
@@ -15,6 +15,15 @@ SECTIONS
     BORINGSSL_bcm_rodata_end = .;
   }

+  /* GCC 14 and later place read-only data that needs a dynamic relocation in
+   * .data.rel.ro.local rather than .rodata. Retain it in its own output
+   * section, outside the integrity-hashed ranges marked above. Output section
+   * matching is first-match-wins, so the broader *(*.data.*) discard below
+   * still catches anything else. */
+  .data.rel.ro.local : {
+    *(.data.rel.ro.local)
+  }
+
   /DISCARD/ : {
     /* These sections shouldn't exist. In order to catch any slip-ups, direct
      * the linker to discard them. */
